  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Past habits",
   "texto": [
    "**Locuiam** means «I lived» or «solía vivir»; **eram**, «era» or «I was». We also use the imperfect for the context of a story.",
    "For a finished experience you already saw the perfect compound: **am fost** («I've been»). Do not confuse **eram** («was / was») with **am fost** («I've been / have been»)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Terminations",
   "texto": [
    "In many verbs, **-am, -ai, -a** terminations help form the imperfect: **locuiam** (I / we lived), **locuiai** (you lived), **locuia** (he / she lived). With **a fi** we use **eram, erai, era**."
   ]
  },
